# Screenshot → code triage (mandatory)

When the user attaches or pastes a **screenshot** of something to fix, do **not** open-ended explore the repo. Resolve a reference point first, then open that file.

## Triage ladder (stop at the first solid hit)

1. **Read the image** for visible chrome text, route clues, and any overlay chips (`planDetail.section.transport`, route path, etc.).
2. **If overlay ids are visible** → copy the short/wire id → `./scripts/agent-ui-source.sh <id>` → open the printed `file:` / `entry:`.
3. **Else match visible label text** → `./scripts/agent-ui-source.sh --label "<text>"` or grep [`docs/agent-ui-map.md`](../../docs/agent-ui-map.md) / `AgentUiIds` key paths.
4. **Else feature is obvious** → open the one [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) feature entry (and domain skill) — not sibling giants.
5. **Else sim is still on that screen** → `./scripts/agent-ui-route.sh` + one `./scripts/agent-ui-dump.sh --prefix ontrack.<feature>` **or** estimate a point and run `./scripts/agent-ui-hit.sh <x> <y>` (logical points) / `--pixel` for screenshot pixels. Then `agent-ui-source.sh` on the hit id.
6. **Still ambiguous** → `./scripts/agent-ui-overlay.sh on`, leave the sim on the surface, capture/read one overlay screenshot, then turn overlay off when done.

## Source of truth pointers

| Pointer | Where |
|---------|--------|
| Wire / key-path ids | `src/utils/agent-ui/ids.ts`, `docs/agent-ui-map.md` |
| Id → files | `docs/agent-ui-sources.json` via `./scripts/agent-ui-source.sh` |
| Routes / flows | `docs/agent-routes.md` |
| Feature entry | `AGENTS.md` table + `.cursor/skills/<domain>/` |

## Rules

- Prefer **id → source** over reading many unrelated screens.
- Hit/overlay coordinates are for **lookup only** — never tap by screenshot coordinates; tap by `ontrack.*` testID.
- If a control/region is missing an id, **add** `AgentUiIds` + `testID` / `AgentTestId` (layout anchors may omit `onPress`) + map row in the same change.
- Do not regenerate the whole sources index unless you added/renamed many ids — then `npm run agent-ui:sources`.

## Do not

- Grep the whole `src/features/` tree hoping to recognize the screenshot.
- Tab-hop or re-seed just to identify a screen when route/dump/hit/overlay fits.
- Treat a screenshot as a substitute for `agent-ui-assert` when the claim is structural.
